# GORILLA OVERRIDE (2026-09-01): this file did not exist, and its absence cost
# three separate bugs in one afternoon.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true — the Windows default — git rewrites LF to CRLF in the
# working tree on checkout. The repository stores LF, so nothing shows up in
# `git diff` and the change is invisible. What it broke:
#
#   1. The prompt files are //go:embed'd, so the line endings present at BUILD
#      time are compiled into the binary. A Windows build shipped a different
#      prompt from a Linux build of identical source. The section splitter then
#      lost the carriage return from every section boundary when it rejoined —
#      24 bytes — and the round-trip guard failed while pointing at correct code.
#      Prompt caching is a prefix match, so this also meant a prompt could not
#      share a cache with itself across builds.
#
#   2. The byte-size guards on the shipped prompts (666, 267) read 678 and 274,
#      firing on the checkout rather than on any edit to the text they protect.
#
#   3. `^depends=\(...\)$` in the PKGBUILD tests never matched, because `$` in Go's
#      multiline regexp matches before `\n` and a CRLF line ends `)\r`. The
#      PKGBUILD declared both `depends=` and `sha256sums=` correctly and the
#      tests reported both as missing.
#
# It also makes `gofmt -l` flag every file in the tree, which is how a real
# formatting problem would hide.
#
# eol=lf, not text=auto alone: `auto` still hands Windows CRLF. This project
# builds a binary whose embedded content must not depend on which machine
# compiled it, so the working tree is LF everywhere.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats — never touch these.
*.png    binary
*.ico    binary
*.svg    text eol=lf
*.syso   binary
*.gz     binary
*.zip    binary
*.db     binary
*.pdf    binary

# Shell scripts and packaging must be LF or they do not run on the target.
*.sh        text eol=lf
PKGBUILD    text eol=lf
*.desktop   text eol=lf

# Go source and the embedded prompt text: LF, so a build is reproducible
# whichever platform it happens on.
*.go   text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
